  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` in `src/core/truncate.ts` and committed it as c04e841. `npm run fast` passed, including the new tests.\n\n- **Behaviour:** the result is at most `max` code points, so astral characters like emoji are never split. If the text is longer than `max`, it keeps both ends around `…`, and the head gets the extra character when the budget is odd. For example, `abcdefghij` with `max` 5 gives `ab…ij`.\n- **Edge cases:** `max` of 1 returns just `…`. `max` of 0 or less returns an empty string.\n- **Reuse:** I didn't reuse any existing helper. The truncation helpers I found are in `scripts/` and `src/worker/`, and `src/core` may only import its own files.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/truncate.test.ts` covers short text, both ends, tiny budgets and emoji. I added a weight of 0.1 for it in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **Commit title:** it has no task id in parentheses. I wasn't given one, so I left it off.",
